     1	"""Portable repository contracts: annotation-free Gherkin facts and binding evidence.
     2	
     3	This module is deliberately separate from :mod:`app.domain.models`, which describes CTA's own
     4	strict fixture artifacts (``@SCN-nnn`` tags, ``# cta:artifact`` annotations, requirement front
     5	matter). An external project must not be forced to adopt those declarations to be indexed, so the
     6	portable path has its own identity scheme:
     7	
     8	* Every identity is prefixed with a repository id, so two repositories that both use
     9	  ``features/login.feature`` and ``@SCN-001`` never collide.
    10	* Identity is derived from the pinned commit plus the source locator, and the strategy is recorded
    11	  (``source_locator``). Nothing claims continuity across edits, renames, or reordering.
    12	* Directly parsed facts, framework-resolved matches, observed executions, and unknown information
    13	  are different fields with different types. There is no field that means "probably works".
    14	
    15	The models carry ``extra="forbid"`` so a query response cannot smuggle an undocumented claim.
