# FT-03 — lifecycle traceability and Gherkin acceptance specifications

**Story:** FT-03 ([#39](https://github.com/anthonygraca/gherkin-knowledge-graph/issues/39)),
sub-issue of [F-01 Foundation, #7](https://github.com/anthonygraca/gherkin-knowledge-graph/issues/7).
**Owner:** shared platform. **Slice:** M0 foundation conventions (maintenance). **Priority:** P0.

**Delivery state:** the specification, the convention documents and the author checks exist; the
owner/team review of the draft intent and of the extracted criteria, and any independent review,
are outstanding. This record claims no approval, no Gherkin execution and no external delivery.

> As a project contributor, I want requirements, story acceptance criteria, implementation and
> verification evidence connected through a documented lifecycle, so that each change has a
> reviewable engineering basis.

The canonical behavioral criteria are in [FT-03.feature](FT-03.feature).

## Source and rationale

The repository owner asked that CTA be developed through the full lifecycle — stakeholder needs,
system obligations, story refinement with Gherkin acceptance criteria, design, implementation,
verification, validation, release and maintenance — with the project's own traceability discipline
exercised as it is expected of its users. The convention is recorded in
[development-lifecycle.md](../development-lifecycle.md); the roadmap carries the delivery-level
statement in *"Developing CTA with its own traceability discipline"*; the draft
[project definition](../project-definition.md) is the first lifecycle artifact. As an
engineering-convention story it traces to that process constraint rather than to a fabricated
end-user requirement (see activity 4 in the lifecycle document).

**Retrospective attribution.** The convention documents and the M0 criteria migration already
existed as working-tree changes before this story was created. The author record
[lifecycle-specification-migration.md](../reviews/lifecycle-specification-migration.md) cites
SETUP-01 (#8), FT-01 (#18) and FT-02 (#19) as the items served at the time it was written; FT-03
is added prospectively and rewrites nothing. No execution, review or approval is inferred for the
earlier work, and the migration does not amend M0's approved exit criteria or its approved
snapshot.

## Scope

| Deliverable | Location | State |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Lifecycle activities, typed trace associations, review points, evidence conventions | [development-lifecycle.md](../development-lifecycle.md) | Convention drafted; review outstanding |
| Intended use, stakeholders, boundary, risks, candidate obligations REQ-101–REQ-108 | [project-definition.md](../project-definition.md) | Draft; no requirement approved |
| Canonical M0 criteria with stable scenario IDs and retained AC labels | [FT-01.feature](FT-01.feature), [FT-02.feature](FT-02.feature) | Migrated with wording preserved; no runner bindings |
| Milestone index keeping scope, rationale and the explicit criterion-to-check mapping | [M0-foundation.md](M0-foundation.md) | Updated; the mapping is not an executed result |
| Story intake asking for source obligations and the canonical specification reference | [.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/user-story.yml](../../.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/user-story.yml) | Updated |
| Conventions pointing at the lifecycle | `AGENTS.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, roadmap, `docs/STATUS.md`, issue map | Updated (attribution/prose only) |
| Author verification record for the migration | [lifecycle-specification-migration.md](../reviews/lifecycle-specification-migration.md) | Author checks; not an independent approval |

## Non-goals

* No Gherkin runner, step bindings, BDD framework or new CI gate. Selecting tooling and binding
  steps needs its own scoped story and an ADR; unbound scenarios are never reported as executed.
* No new product behavior, API, contract, fixture or schema change, and no later-milestone work.
* No requirement approval: REQ-101–REQ-108 remain discussion candidates for owner/team review.
* No retroactive scenario IDs in historical execution records; earlier run records keep the
  revision and labels they were produced under.
* No automated traceability gate, parser or database; the verification map stays Markdown.
* No graph, vector-store, model-provider or benchmark-tooling choice, and no self-ingestion
  before the product supports it.

## Dependencies and prerequisites

| Dependency | State at this point |
| --- | --- |
| M0 independent approval | Applies to its named snapshots (`bca69cf`, oracle attestation) only; this story is outside it |
| M0 landing | PR #38 merged as `efa824b`; closing #18/#19 is a team action and remains open |
| Commit-reference slice (SETUP-01, #8) | Prepared in the working tree, uncommitted; it sets the commit format this story's commit uses |
| Review of [project-definition.md](../project-definition.md) and the REQ-101–REQ-108 allocations | Outstanding; no approval is recorded |
| Research report ([continuous-traceability-research-report.md](../continuous-traceability-research-report.md)) | Referenced as context; its hypotheses and proposed comparison are not results. Its tracker attribution is [#40](https://github.com/anthonygraca/gherkin-knowledge-graph/issues/40) (F-10 research-planning task); it grants no technology or schema decision. |

## Verification map

Methods P1–P4 are throwaway analysis scripts recorded in this file (see *Local verification
record*); P5 is recorded inspection. None of them is a Gherkin runner execution. A mapping or a
recorded author check is not an engineering approval.

| Scenario | Method | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| SCN-401 | P5: inspect the M0 index for canonical-scenario links instead of scenario blocks, and the issue form fields | *Local verification record* |
| SCN-402 | P1: compare every migrated scenario with the M0 record at `efa824b5`, including the retained labels and counts | *Local verification record* |
| SCN-403 | P2: parse the mapping table; resolve every selector against `backend/tests/` | *Local verification record* |
| SCN-404 | P3: run the same P2 procedure against a deliberately broken copy of the map | *Local verification record* |
| SCN-405 | P5: quote the status statements and confirm the absence of execution/approval claims | *Local verification record* |
| SCN-406 | P4: collect the tags of every canonical feature file | *Local verification record* |

## Open review obligations

* Owner/team review of the draft [project definition](../project-definition.md) and the
  candidate obligations, including any risk/control ownership; nothing is approved yet.
* Review of the extracted FT-01/FT-02 wording and of these FT-03 criteria, and acceptance of the
  mapping's meaning and adequacy — the author checks are structural and do not establish that.
* If these conventions are to become an approved baseline, review by someone other than the
  author, covering the workstream boundaries the conventions touch (A, B, C).
* Stakeholder validation: demonstrate following one criterion to its mapped check and back, and
  record the result separately from implementation verification.
* Landing the change through a pull request whose body carries the specification links and the
  remaining obligations; M0 tracker closure (#18/#19) stays a separate team action.

